From 2855fd284033fe57250c5f999ec17c6c7c0b4b7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:17:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sx8-int8 attempt E: 16-value activation scales for the S-X8
 int8 cm1 kernel (env-only arm)

GGML_ARIFI_SX8_CM1_H16=1: quantize_q8_1 HALF=1 stores one scale per 16-value half (ds = d0, d1); the SX8_H16 cm1
kernel keeps one int32 accumulator per half (TK == 16, K_SUB == 2) with its own B scale, and the min term uses the
exact half sums (m * (d0*s0 + d1*s1)). Replaces the two-digit route for S-X8 while on; refused unless int8 coopmat
K == 16. Offline gate on 25 captured real inputs: error energy x0.51..0.72, worst token x0.64..0.79 vs 32-value
scales. Default unchanged (fix B). RED twin matmul_sx8hred_q8_1 for the tests.

Lane: sx8-int8-stage10-2026-10-02

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
